      "report_date": "2026-11-23",
      "title": "Attempts to Disable Domestic Security Products via BYOVD: Beware of Malware Distributed Disguised as Legitimate AI Tools",
      "summary": "Attackers distributed malware disguised as a legitimate AI tool installer, with a Korean-language fake download site, to target users in South Korea. The malware dropped the vulnerable NeacSafe64.sys anti-cheat driver, which carries CVE-2025-45737, and used it to load a malicious kernel driver named WinWyvern. The attackers reused a publicly available proof-of-concept exploit with only minor changes. WinWyvern patches memory in domestic security products to disable file detection and blocking, which could allow follow-on malware to run undetected. It can also execute additional payloads from its C2 server. AhnLab notes that the latest version of its V3 Lite product is not affected by these memory patches and can detect and remediate the attack chain.",
      "completeness": "Medium",
      "threats": [
        "Byovd_technique"
      ],
      "geo": [
        "Korea"
      ],
      "ttp_tactics": 1,
      "ttp_techniques": 0,
