    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-23",
      "title": "Agentic Attacks: In The Wild",
      "summary": "Agentic offensive frameworks such as ARTEX, Cairn, CyberStrikeAI and HexStrike are driving a surge in cloud intrusions, with Wiz reporting a 3x rise in engagement requests. These tools are open source, with hundreds of forks, and activity attributed to ARTEX comes from multiple unrelated operators rather than one campaign or actor. Attacks are noisy and opportunistic, using residential proxy rotation, password spraying, and probing of sign-up, identity-provider, and CI/CD paths across many organizations. One documented intrusion chained compromised VCS credentials and a stolen service-account token into cluster-admin access. Exposed ARTEX consoles and open directories revealed operator workflows and harvested AI provider keys, and keys stolen from one platform often enabled attacks on the next. Defenders are advised to rely on behavioral detections for speed, breadth and systematic structure, since tool-specific rules are perishable.",
      "completeness": "Low",
      "threats": [
