    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-23",
      "title": "OXLoader abuses DLL hijacking to distribute different malware families",
      "summary": "OXLoader is a loader that installs other malware, and Malwarebytes reports increased activity involving it after Elastic first documented it in June 2026. The payloads observed include Remcos, OverLord, PureRAT, Lunex Stealer, LOLD, and Hermes, which can steal browser passwords or grant remote control of Windows PCs. Attackers distribute it through malicious ZIP files disguised as complaint or copyright-infringement notices, fake software activators, and cracks hosted on GitLab. A key new feature is DLL hijacking, in which legitimate executables from Microsoft, Steam, OBS Studio, and PDF or Word readers load trojanized DLLs to decrypt and run OXLoader. Defenders should be wary of copyright-themed emails, executables with long names or double extensions, and downloaded activators or cracks.",
      "completeness": "Medium",
      "threats": [
