    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-23",
      "title": "From Game Cheats to NWHStealer: Following a Rust Loader Infection Chain",
      "summary": "NWHStealer is delivered through game cheat and utility lures, including fake FiveM, Valorant, and Fortnite cheats, Lua script executors, and a Discord mass-DM tool, hosted on GitLab and GitHub. Several downloader families (.NET PowerShell, Go, and a Delphi dropper) fetch a Rust loader the researchers track as WarpLoader. WarpLoader uses module stomping, ETW bypass through hardware breakpoints, and indirect syscalls to inject the stealer into Chromium-based browsers. The stealer harvests browser credentials, cookies, wallet data, Discord and Telegram data, and AI developer-tool credentials. The researchers assess that the campaign targets individuals such as game enthusiasts rather than enterprises, but it poses risks to shared and BYOD devices used for gaming.",
      "completeness": "Medium",
      "threats": [
