    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-23",
      "title": "13 Malicious NuGet Packages Target .NET Developers With Fake Job Assessments",
      "summary": "Socket identified 13 malicious NuGet packages, published from July to November 2026, that are tied to fake \"Home Assessment\" take-home projects aimed at Windows .NET developers. The packages pose as WinUI 3 and WPF button controls, and building or running a project that uses them downloads files from GitHub, side-loads a DLL through osk.exe, or runs an executable. One package, WinUI.Button 1.0.0, remains listed on NuGet, while NuGet removed the other 12. The operation also uses fake axios repositories, npm packages, a ClickFix page and a trojanized crypto wallet app, with GitHub serving as staging and command-and-control infrastructure. The report does not attribute the campaign to a named actor, though it resembles North Korean fake-interview lures. Defenders should treat take-home projects as untrusted code and check for the listed packages and artifacts.",
