      "title": "ARTEX leads to persistent ZQAgent backdoor",
      "summary": "ZQAgent is a new stealthy backdoor, deployed by the FOG0003 actor using the LLM-driven ARTEX tool during an NVISO incident response engagement. Unlike typical smash-and-grab LLM intrusions, it gives operators a long-lasting foothold, which NVISO believes reflects operator-specific instructions rather than autonomous behavior. The backdoor hides by migrating into an anonymous memory file and spoofing a dbus-daemon process, and it encrypts its configuration and network traffic. It persists through both systemd services and cron jobs, with ZQAgent reportedly observed in Belgium and Taiwan and likely used in Asia against government and human-rights organizations. NVISO warns that LLM use will likely spread to ransomware and espionage, so defenders should harden perimeters and shorten response times, including considering automated asset isolation.",
